漏洞 CVE-2025-58754 具体是什么？ 可能是 axios 1.7.4 之前? 需要知道。CVE-2025-58754 可能 axios 在 Node.js 中处理 data: URLs 时，fromDataURI 将 data URI 转为 Buffer，如果 data URI 很大导致内存耗尽？ 触发条件：在 Node.js 中应用将外部可控的超大 data: URL 传给 axios 发起 GET 请求。前提：运行 Node.js；请求 URL 使用 data: scheme 且请求方法为 GET；应用未对外部 URL 的大小或 scheme 做限制。 漏洞函数：Blob, Buffer, axios, axios.get, axios.request, fromDataURI, maxBodyLength, maxContentLength. 这听起来 axios 的 http adapter? 当 URL 是 data:，axios 在 Node 中可能用 fromDataURI 转换到 buffer，受 maxBodyLength/maxContentLength 限制? CVE 可能是 DoS via data URL causing memory consumption before maxBodyLength? 需要最终 URL data scheme.

代码中 internal.get(req.query.path) with baseURL. 如果 path 是 data: URL, buildFullPath maybe combine. 但 axios 1.7.4 的 isAbsoluteURL? Let's verify from memory: axios v1 has helpers/isAbsoluteURL.js:
export default function isAbsoluteURL(url) {
  return /^([a-z][a-z\d\+\-\.]*:)?\/\//i.test(url);
}
So only protocol-relative or absolute with //, not data:. buildFullPath:
export default function buildFullPath(baseURL, requestedURL) {
  if (baseURL && !isAbsoluteURL(requestedURL)) {
    return combineURLs(baseURL, requestedURL);
  }
  return requestedURL;
}
So data: not absolute, combined. But wait, if requestedURL contains data: and no //, it is relative, combine. The final URL is http://10.0.0.8:8080/data:... . Then in http adapter, parse url: new URL('http://10.0.0.8:8080/data:text/plain;base64,AAAA')? URL parses path as /data:text/plain;base64,AAAA? The colon in path is allowed? Yes. So not data.

But if attacker passes path=//data:text/plain,? isAbsoluteURL true? //... then final URL //data:...? In browsers, protocol-relative; in Node URL? new URL('//data:text/plain', baseURL?) But axios with baseURL? buildFullPath returns requestedURL if absolute. Then config.url = '//data:text/plain'. http adapter maybe uses new URL(config.url) which throws? Or http.request with path? Not data scheme. If path=data:...? no.

Could attacker pass path=http://10.0.0.8:8080/data:...? isAbsoluteURL true because //, final URL http://... path /data:... not data. No.

Could attacker pass path=data:...//? No scheme still data but no //, not absolute, combine. final http://.../data:...//. Not data.

Thus strict premise not satisfied due to baseURL. But is there any way for req.query.path to override baseURL? In axios, if requestedURL is absolute according to isAbsoluteURL, it overrides. To override with data scheme, URL must match isAbsoluteURL? data: does not. So no.

